ink: [DB-9437](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-9437)\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhile adding tests for #17942, it was observed that in one rare case, this hash lookup was not returning the right results, causing weird test failures:\r\n```\r\nYbPgInheritsCacheEntry entry = hash_search(\r\n\t\tYbPgInheritsCache, (void *)&parentOid, HASH_ENTER, &found);\r\n```\r\nThe root cause is this initialization code:\r\n```\r\n\tHASHCTL ctl = {0};\r\n\tctl.keysize = sizeof(Oid);\r\n\tctl.entrysize = sizeof(YbPgInheritsCacheEntryData);\r\n\tctl.hcxt = CacheMemoryContext;\r\n\tYbPgInheritsCache =\r\n\t\thash_create(\"YbPgInheritsCache\", 8, &ctl, HASH_ELEM | HASH_CONTEXT);\r\n```\r\nThis does not specify any hash function or comparator during initialization. This means, by default, string comparison is used:\r\n```\r\n/*\r\n\t * If you don't specify a match function, it defaults to string_compare if\r\n\t * you used string_hash (either explicitly or by default) and to memcmp\r\n\t * otherwise.\r\n\t */\r\n\tif (flags & HASH_COMPARE)\r\n\t\thashp->match = info->match;\r\n\telse if (hashp->hash == string_hash)\r\n\t\thashp->match = (HashCompareFunc) string_compare;\r\n\telse\r\n\t\thashp->match = memcmp;\r\n```\r\nWe should not use string comparison for YbPgInheritsCache because its key is of type Oid. String comparison is mainly used for null terminated strings and will fail for binary data comparison. The fix for this issue is to use \r\n```\r\nYbPgInheritsCache =\r\n\t\thash_create(\"YbPgInheritsCache\", 8, &ctl, HASH_ELEM | HASH_BLOBS | HASH_CONTEXT);\r\n```\r\nThis is what all other PG code using Oid as hash key uses. See comments in dynahash.c which explains why:\r\n```\r\n* dynahash.c provides support for these types of lookup keys:\r\n *\r\n * 1. Null-terminated C strings (truncated if necessary to fit in keysize),\r\n * compared as though by strcmp().  This is the default behavior.\r\n *\r\n * 2. Arbitrary binary data of size keysize, compared as though by memcmp().\r\n * (Caller must ensure there are no undefined padding bits in the keys!)\r\n * This is selected by specifying HASH_BLOBS flag to hash_create.\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Issue Type\r\n\r\nkind/bug\r\n\r\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\r\n\r\n- [X] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\r\n\r\n[DB-9437]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-9437?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/20436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/20436/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":11392976843,"node_id":"REFE_lADOBlCVUc5p042gzwAAAAKnEwfL","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/events/11392976843","actor":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"referenc